 "notes": "Section starts p.63 row 5 under the overline. p.65 actually has 9 printed rows (not 7 as the brief says); I read all 9, ending with 'ren en àri āa - s' / 'The name of its doorkeeper is'; the brief's 'row 7' sic (unen ṭep - f) is my row 9, its 'row 1' blank is row 1. p.66 stops after Semati (row 6). Overlines: each pylon's opening runs t'eṭet...àn (àn is under the line in halls 1,2,4,5,6); hall 3 overline covers t'eṭet χeft sper (p.64 row 7) and er sebχet χemt ent (row 8) and then a separate short overline over àn; pa/Àusàr are not overlined; hall 3 has no t'et before àn. Hall 6 overline continues from p.66 row 1 onto row 2 covering saset and àn. The narrow upright with small bumps on one side (qat, āa, āāau, āāat, ābt, reχ-tu, qeṭ, śas, θennu) coded Y1a throughout. Thin flat sign with tab at right but no curled end = D36; low flat sign with curled left end = U15. Ani's determinative varies: A52 (p.63, p.64 twice), none (p.65 row 4), A1 (p.65 row 7, p.66 row 2). Àusàr is always Q2+D4 with no god figure. Budge's English for ī is in braces '{the traveller along [the way].}'."
